# Conventions

> Generated by scafoldercli. Conventions are enforced by review, lint and tests.
> If a rule here no longer matches the code, fix one of the two.

## Naming

- Files: `kebab-case.ts`.
- Classes and types: `PascalCase`.
- Variables, functions and methods: `camelCase`.
- Constants that are true configuration: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`.
- Test files sit next to the code they test and end in `.spec.ts`.

## Imports

- Use relative imports inside a module, and the module's public entry point
  (`index.ts`) when importing across modules.
- Never reach into another module's internal files.
- Never import upward across a dependency rule listed in `ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Group imports: node builtins, external packages, internal modules.

## File organization

- One exported concept per file.
- A module owns its own types; shared types live in `shared/`.
- Nothing lands in `shared/` until it is used by at least two modules.

## Error handling

- Throw typed, domain-specific errors; never bare `Error` with a string.
- Translate domain errors into HTTP responses at the edge, not in the domain.
- Never swallow an error. If a failure is expected, model it in the return type.
- Error responses never include stack traces, SQL, or internal identifiers.

## Logging

- Log through the shared logger; never `console.log`.
- Log structured fields, not interpolated sentences.
- Never log secrets, tokens, passwords or full request bodies.

## Configuration

- All configuration comes from environment variables, validated at startup.
- The process refuses to start when required configuration is missing.
- `.env.example` lists every variable. `.env` is never committed.
<% if (it.hasTests) { -%>

## Testing

- Runner: <%= it.config.testing %>.
- Unit tests cover behaviour, not implementation details.
- Every bug fix starts with a failing test.
- Tests must not depend on execution order or on a shared mutable database row.
<% } -%>
<% if (it.hasDatabase) { -%>

## Database

- Engine: <%= it.config.database %>, accessed through <%= it.config.orm %>.
- Schema changes go through migrations; never edit the database by hand.
- Migrations are forward-only and reviewed like code.
<% if (it.hasRepository) { -%>
- Domain and application code depends on repository interfaces, never on
  <%= it.config.orm %> types.
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
<% if (it.hasAuth) { -%>

## Authentication

- Passwords are hashed with Argon2id; plaintext passwords are never stored or logged.
- Access tokens are short-lived; refresh tokens are stored server-side, rotated
  on every use, and revocable.
- A reused refresh token invalidates the whole session family.
<% } -%>

## Commits

- One logical change per commit.
- Conventional Commits: `type(scope): summary` — `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`,
  `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`.
- The test suite passes on every commit.
